// D1 round 11 / X1, the FALLBACK direction — a call result with NO SUMMARY.
//
// X1's new arm answers "what does this call's result reborrow?" from the
// callee's `to_result` mask. The arm's safety argument is that it is STRICTLY
// ADDITIVE: where no summary exists — the pre-mono generic pass (`flows_` is
// null), an extern / metaprog stub / body-less callee, or a call the mangled
// symbol cannot resolve, as here through a `dyn` receiver — `by_mask` returns
// without seeding and the pre-X1 syntactic answer (`{}` for a Call) stands.
// This fixture spells that shape and must COMPILE.
//
// ⚠ WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT. It is a ROUTE witness, not a verdict
// discriminator: no revert of the X1 arm can red it, because the arm's whole
// contract on this path is to do nothing. Constructing a verdict that separates
// "seed nothing" from "seed every argument" needs the seeded loan to DIE at a
// different point than the true one, which this model (element-insensitive,
// loan charged to the holder's root) cannot express. So the route is proved the
// only way it can be: a fire counter INSIDE the null-summary branch of
// `by_mask`, on an otherwise identical build. MEASURED that way, per file:
//
//   this file                     : arm entered 1, no-summary exit 1, seed 0
//   fail/…x1_prospective_alias    : entered 2, no-summary 0, summary 1, seed 1
//   fail/…x1_result_subplace      : entered 2, no-summary 0, summary 1, seed 1
//   fail/…x2_byvalue_result       : entered 2, no-summary 0, summary 1, seed 1
//
// so the `d.get()` below IS the no-summary exit (a `dyn` receiver resolves to
// no callee) and the three refusal witnesses are the other exit. Over the
// stdlib the same arm sees 675 calls of which 470 carry a summary, so this
// route is the majority one there too. The counter was removed and the
// restored sources are md5-identical to the pre-instrumentation ones.
package bc_d1r11_x1_nosummary_admit;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;
#[borrow_carrying]
struct B { p: &i64 }
struct C { v: i64 }
impl C {
    fn mk(&self) -> B { return B { p: &self.v }; }
    fn bump(&mut self) { self.v = self.v + 1i64; }
}
trait Src { fn get(&mut self) -> &mut Vec<B>; }
struct Own { own: Vec<B> }
impl Src for Own { fn get(&mut self) -> &mut Vec<B> { return &mut self.own; } }
fn main() -> i64 {
    let mut c: C = C { v: 1i64 };
    let mut o: Own = Own { own: Vec::<B>::new() };
    let d: &mut dyn Src = &mut o;
    let s: &mut Vec<B> = d.get();    // no summary: dyn dispatch
    let n: i64 = s.len();
    c.bump();                        // must be ADMITTED
    return c.v + n;
}
